          {
            title: 'Tute corriente',
            subtitle: 'Card Game',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Tute corriente is the oldest two-player form of Tute from Spain. Six cards each, 13th face up for trump, rest as stock. No follow suit until stock is empty; then must follow and beat or trump. First to 101 points or tute (four kings or horses) wins.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: "Tute corriente is the oldest two-player form of Tute. Tute originated in Italy as tutti, spread to Spain in the 19th century with returning troops, and became one of Spain's most popular card games; the two-player corriente form is the traditional variant described in Spanish card-game literature.",
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            title: 'Setup',
            subtitle: 'Table, deck, equipment, and deal',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Two players, each playing for themselves; no partnerships.',
